<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="113" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Author Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 (L2 repeatable deploy script, C5.9/C1.7)</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-1 -- Foundation</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New script authoring parity with the existing Deploy-BffApi.ps1 pattern, no existing-file .cs modification. STANDARD per root CLAUDE.md §8 table.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical script authoring following an established sibling pattern (Deploy-BffApi.ps1) -- Sonnet @ high.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>100, 101, 108, 109</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, deploy, azure-deployment</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Author scripts/Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 in parity with scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1's shape: dotnet publish (linux-x64 framework-dependent) for BOTH .Api and .Worker projects -&gt; az webapp deploy (zip) to their respective App Service targets -&gt; post-deploy verification (healthz on both sites + the C4.6/task 108 queue-property check via az servicebus queue show + config fail-fast confirmation that NFR-05-required keys are present in each site's resolved app settings). This is the delivery vehicle for task 102's dispatcher and converges the currently-ad-hoc-deployed live binary (ahead of committed source per DS-5's B.6 gap) with committed source.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in PowerShell deploy-script authoring, dotnet publish for linux-x64 App Service targets, and az webapp deploy zip-deploy semantics.</role>

  <goal>scripts/Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 exists, accepts -Environment (dev/prod) and -Target (Api|Worker|Both) parameters, publishes + zip-deploys the named target(s), and runs a post-deploy verification block: /healthz 200 on each deployed site, az servicebus queue show confirms sessions+dedup ON (task 108's properties), and a config-presence check confirms the NFR-05 fail-fast keys (Cosmos:AccountEndpoint, ServiceBus:FullyQualifiedNamespace, ManagedIdentity:ClientId) are non-empty in the deployed site's live app settings.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-5 §C5.9 confirms zero L2 deploy tooling exists today (grep -i controlplane scripts/ .github/workflows/ returns 0 hits) -- the live dev stamp has been deployed ad-hoc, ahead of committed source. DS-4's Wave G-1 content explicitly lists this script as part of the foundation wave, parity with Deploy-BffApi.ps1. Because task 100 split the project into .Api/.Worker, this script MUST target both (Worker has no slot -- deploy = stop -&gt; zip-deploy -&gt; start per DS-3 §3, the honest drain story since no platform gives a graceful 60-min drain).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">scripts/Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="100" status="pending">.Api/.Worker projects must exist as publish targets</dependency>
      <dependency task="101" status="pending">Worker App Service resource must exist as a deploy target</dependency>
      <dependency task="108" status="pending">Queue properties this script's verification step checks must exist</dependency>
      <dependency task="109" status="pending">Config keys this script verifies must match the corrected Bicep-emitted keys</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="DS-3 §3 Option 2">Worker deploy semantics: NO staging slot -- stop -&gt; zip-deploy -&gt; start. Api KEEPS staging slot + swap (existing Deploy-BffApi.ps1-style slot-swap pattern applies to Api only).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Three-question component-justification gate applies to any NEW class/interface/Bicep resource/script this task introduces. Existing/Extension/Cost-of-doing-nothing are pre-answered in &lt;notes&gt; below; cite them verbatim in the PR description per root CLAUDE.md §11 enforcement table.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 authoring</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds3-api-worker-split.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds5-cat456-remediation.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="BFF deploy script parity" location="scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1">publish -&gt; az webapp deploy -&gt; post-deploy verification shape this script mirrors for L2's two App Service targets.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (STANDARD). Read Deploy-BffApi.ps1 in full.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Publish block">dotnet publish -c Release -r linux-x64 --self-contained false for the named target project(s).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Api deploy">az webapp deploy --type zip against the .Api staging slot, then (optionally, behind a -Swap switch) SwapSlotAsync-equivalent az webapp deployment slot swap.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Worker deploy">az webapp stop -&gt; az webapp deploy --type zip -&gt; az webapp start against the slotless Worker site.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify healthz">curl/Invoke-RestMethod against both sites' /healthz -- expect 200.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Verify queue">az servicebus queue show --query 'requiresSession,requiresDuplicateDetection' -- expect true/true (task 108's properties).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Verify config">Query each site's resolved app settings (az webapp config appsettings list) for the presence (non-empty) of Cosmos:AccountEndpoint / ServiceBus:FullyQualifiedNamespace / ManagedIdentity:ClientId (accounting for Bicep's __ delimiter).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Exit codes">Script exits non-zero on ANY verification failure, with a clear message identifying which check failed.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the config-presence verification (step 6) finds a KEY MISSING that task 109 was supposed to fix, STOP and escalate rather than deploying anyway — a missing NFR-05 key means the site will fail fast at its own boot per the existing IOptions validation, and shipping it anyway just moves the failure discovery later.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">publish</tool>
    <tool name="az webapp">deploy/stop/start/config appsettings list</tool>
    <tool name="az servicebus">queue show</tool>
    <tool name="curl">healthz verification</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="script">scripts/Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">scripts/Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 exists and supports -Target Api|Worker|Both.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Running it against dev with -Target Both completes with exit code 0 when both sites are healthy post-deploy.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The script's post-deploy verification block fails (non-zero exit) when injected with a deliberately-broken app-setting (manual smoke test during authoring) -- confirms the check is load-bearing, not decorative.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'healthz' Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 shows the verification call for BOTH deployed sites.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'requiresSession\|requiresDuplicateDetection' Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 shows the queue-property verification step.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- Deploy-BffApi.ps1 is the proven sibling pattern for App Service publish+deploy+verify; nothing new to invent mechanically. Extension -- this script extends that pattern to L2's two-site topology (Api+Worker) with L2-specific verification steps (queue properties, NFR-05 keys) the BFF script has no equivalent for. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- without a repeatable deploy script, every subsequent Wave G task that needs a live deploy (dispatcher smoke test, sidecar verification, H13 live probes) repeats ad-hoc az commands, perpetuating the exact 'live binary ahead of committed source' drift DS-5 flags today.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
